```
if (index <0... ) return;
if (index === this.weaponIndex) {
  if (silent) { this.viewmodel.visible = this.visible; }
  return;
}
```
But reset uses before `this.visible=true`; we set visible after. Could just call `this.switchWeapon(0,true);` and it returns; then `this.weapon.model.group.visible=true`? viewmodel points maybe current (could not 0 from prior run). Actually if current 0 returns and viewmodel is 0; all groups hidden; then set viewmodel.visible true at end. Good. If current !=0, switch. Fine. So fix select->switch.

